.TH VMINV 1 "2026" "vminv 0.3" "vminv Manual"
.SH NAME
vminv \- read-only VMware vSphere pre-migration inventory & assessment
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vminv
[\fIscan\fR] [\fIoptions\fR]
.br
.B vminv
\fIcommand\fR [\fIargs\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vminv
performs a strictly read-only inventory and migration-readiness assessment of a
VMware vSphere environment, producing machine-readable tables (CSV + JSON) and a
human-readable report. It never creates, modifies, powers, reconfigures,
snapshots, or deletes anything in vCenter.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B scan
Collect inventory, utilization, and migration blockers (the default command).
.TP
.B configure \fR[\fIprofile\fR]
Interactively create/update a named profile (aws-cli style). No secrets are stored.
.TP
.B profiles \fR[show \fIprofile\fR]
List profiles, or print one (secrets redacted).
.TP
.B upload \fIdir\fR [\fB--dest\fR \fIurl\fR]
Ship a run directory to a destination (s3://, gs://, az://, sftp://, https://, path).
.TP
.B schedule \fRadd|list|remove|run
Manage a cron job that scans and uploads on a schedule.
.TP
.B upgrade \fR[\fB--repo\fR \fIowner/name\fR] [\fB--check\fR]
Self-update from GitHub Releases.
.TP
.B completion \fRbash|zsh|fish
Print a shell completion script.
.TP
.B version | help
Print version, or help (\fBvminv help \fIcommand\fR for per-command help).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-profile " " \fINAME\fR
Use a configured profile.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Read-only login + list one object, then exit.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-perf
Skip the utilization pass.
.TP
.B \-\-target " " \fIaws|azure|gcp\fR
Cloud target for analysis and right-sizing.
.TP
.BR \-\-datacenter ", " \-\-cluster ", " \-\-folder ", " \-\-vm " " \fIGLOB\fR
Scope filters.
.TP
.B \-\-output " " \fIDIR\fR
Base output directory.
.TP
.B \-\-dest " " \fIURL\fR
Upload destination for this run.
.TP
.B \-\-format " " \fItable|json\fR
Final summary format on stdout (json is machine-readable).
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet ", " \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Decrease / increase log verbosity.
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-color ", " \-\-no\-progress
Disable color / progress output. \fBNO_COLOR\fR is also honored.
.TP
.BR \-C ", " \-\-config " " \fIFILE\fR
Load a specific config file instead of a profile.
.TP
.B \-\-fixtures " " \fIDIR\fR
Offline: read canned JSON instead of contacting vCenter.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Generic runtime error.
.TP
.B 2
Usage / bad arguments.
.TP
.B 3
Connectivity or authentication failure.
.TP
.B 4
Completed with partial data (some objects unreadable).
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted (SIGINT).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B VCENTER_PASSWORD
vCenter password (alternative to prompt / OS keyring). Never logged.
.TP
.B VMINV_PROFILE
Default profile name.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
If set, disables colored output.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/vminv/profiles/<name>.env
Named profiles (mode 600, no secrets).
.SH SECURITY
Strictly read-only against vCenter. The password is supplied via environment,
OS keyring, or prompt and is never written to logs, profiles, or output.
.SH SEE ALSO
Project README and docs/ for the full data dictionary and design.
